      "content": "It's completely understandable why you feel like the math doesn't work; the weight of that reality is immense. But sometimes, the only thing that feels like a \"fix\" is just stopping the constant fight against the weight. Instead of trying to fix the whole broken thing, maybe you could just focus on making the next few minutes feel a little less heavy. Let the exhaustion be the reason you rest, not the reason you keep pushing.",
